findings.evidence:
analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/OneDoorIntoCrossPlatformAnalyzerTests.cs:327-340 and analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/OneDoorIntoPerOsAnalyzerTests.cs:318-331 each declare `const string abstractions = "}

namespace AgentGuard.Abstractions.Contracts
{
" + "    public interface IPlatformServices { }

" + "    public static class Holder
    {
" + "        public static object Typed() => typeof(IPlatformServices);

" + "        public static IPlatformServices Held => null!;
    }";` then call `SharedAnalyzerSources.EngineCompilation(CrossPlatformUsing/PerOsUsing, SharedAnalyzerSources.InertContainerFactory, abstractions)`. `diff` of the two five-line const bodies (CrossPlatform 331-335 vs PerOs 322-326) returns exit 0 — byte-identical, not merely 'same logic with renamed variables'. The `usings` argument that differs by name (`CrossPlatformUsing` vs `PerOsUsing`) is not even a real variation: both constants hold the identical literal `"using AgentGuard.CrossPlatform;"` (OneDoorIntoCrossPlatformAnalyzerTests.cs:84, OneDoorIntoPerOsAnalyzerTests.cs:58), and the `abstractions` block does not use that using anyway (it opens its own `namespace AgentGuard.Abstractions.Contracts` block and references `IPlatformServices` unqualified within it). So the two composed fixture sources are identical in every byte, with zero parametrization required to unify them — a stricter case than any of the six sibling fixture-shapes (`InsideContainerFactory`, `InsideOtherContainerMethod`, `InsideOtherEngineClass`, `InsideLambdaInContainerFactory`, `InsideLocalFunctionInContainerFactory`, `EngineHolder`) that this same round already extracted into `SharedAnalyzerSources.cs` for precisely this 'both AG0023 and AG0029 need it' reason (confirmed via grep: each of those six is defined once in SharedAnalyzerSources.cs and called from both OneDoorInto* files, e.g. `InsideOtherEngineClass(` at SharedAnalyzerSources.cs:441 with call sites at OneDoorIntoCrossPlatformAnalyzerTests.cs:210 and OneDoorIntoPerOsAnalyzerTests.cs:208). `SharedAnalyzerSources.cs`'s own docstring states its purpose is exactly 'a byte-identical fixture is not spelled twice', and no `Abstractions...` member exists there (confirmed: `grep -n "IPlatformServices Held" analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/*.cs` returns only these two files, nothing in SharedAnalyzerSources.cs).

findings.fix:
Add one field to analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/SharedAnalyzerSources.cs, e.g. `internal static readonly string AbstractionsTypeReferenceSource = EngineCompilation("using AgentGuard.CrossPlatform;", InertContainerFactory, "}

namespace AgentGuard.Abstractions.Contracts
{
    public interface IPlatformServices { }

    public static class Holder
    {
        public static object Typed() => typeof(IPlatformServices);

        public static IPlatformServices Held => null!;
    }");` and have both OneDoorIntoCrossPlatformAnalyzerTests.cs:326-341 and OneDoorIntoPerOsAnalyzerTests.cs:317-332 delete their local `abstractions`/`source` construction and call `Assert.Empty(await RunFromEngineAsync(SharedAnalyzerSources.AbstractionsTypeReferenceSource));` directly.

