" + "        internal static object Nothing() => null!;";` then `SharedAnalyzerSources.EngineHolder(USING_CONST, documented)`, again differing only by the substituted type/member names. The same root-cause pattern recurs a third and fourth time within a single file: EngineInternalsOneDoorAnalyzerTests.cs:126-134 (`EngineInternalInBaseList_FromGatedConsumer_IsReported`, `const string derived = "internal sealed class Derived : EngineInternal
{
}";`) and :136-147 (`ContainerInBaseList_FromGatedConsumer_IsReported`, the same line with `SystemServices` substituted), both feeding the file's own local `Consumer(...)` helper — the identical parametrize-by-type-name gap, unaddressed by a local helper even though both call sites live in the same class.

